    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **56 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**, including the new `Cp45Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature for the `POST /api/owners` create endpoint (read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`). The request may now carry a `title` (`MR`/`MRS`/`MS`/`DR`), and the response returns `salutation = title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `title` (enum, editable) to the `OwnerFields` schema and a read-only derived `salutation` field to the `Owner` schema. The DTOs are generated from this spec.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `title` column with getter/setter, so the title survives create \u2192 persist \u2192 GET.\n\n3. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `title` column to the `owners` table (tests run on hsqldb; the others kept consistent).\n\n4. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added the `salutation` mapping via a `composeSalutation(owner)` default method that concatenates title + space + lastName, falling back to lastName alone when the title is null/blank. MapStruct maps the request title (enum \u2192 String) into the entity and echoes it back automatically.\n\nNo new function classes were needed \u2014 the value is a pure derivation of persisted fields, so it fits the existing response-mapper pattern (like `displayName`/`initials`) rather than a new pipeline step.",
